# Commit Messages

Full standard: `docs/standards/commit-messages.md`

**Only commit when the user explicitly asks.**

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary ≤72 chars>

[body — why, not what]

Task: {plan-id}
```

## Types

`feat` · `fix` · `docs` · `style` · `refactor` · `test` · `chore` · `perf` · `build` · `ci`

## Scopes

`auth` · `clients` · `projects` · `invoices` · `portal` · `admin` · `layout` · `deps` · `test`

## Rules

- Imperative summary: "add hook" not "added hook"
- Match message to `git diff` — read diff before writing
- One task ID per commit when working from development-plan
- Never commit `.env` or secrets
- Use HEREDOC for `git commit -m`

## Examples

```
feat(auth): add LoginPage with form validation

Task: A-05
```

```
test(clients): add useClientList MSW hook tests

Task: C-02
```
